# Security

## Secrets

- Read secrets from `process.env` only; never hardcode or log them.
- `httpLogger` redacts `password`/`token` - keep any new sensitive fields redacted too.
- Never commit `.env`; only `.env.example` is tracked.

## Auth

- Protect routes with the `auth` middleware ([server/src/middleware/auth.js](server/src/middleware/auth.js)).
- JWTs are signed/verified with `process.env.JWT_SECRET`; read the identity from `req.user`.

## Passwords

- Hash passwords with `bcryptjs` in a model pre-save hook.
- Strip `password` in the model `toJSON`; never return it in a response.

## Rate Limiting

Reuse the scoped limiters in [server/src/middleware/rateLimiter.js](server/src/middleware/rateLimiter.js):
`loginLimiter`, `commentLimiter`, `generateLimiter`, `apiLimiter`. Attach sensitive or expensive endpoints to an appropriate limiter.

## Input / Output Safety

- Keep `helmet` and `cors` enabled; the CORS origin is allowlisted via `CLIENT_URL`.
- Validate request input in `src/validators/`.
- On the client, sanitize any user- or AI-generated HTML with `dompurify` before rendering (e.g. blog content/markdown).
